From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MrPowerGamerBR <git@mrpowergamerbr.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:50:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SparklyPaper: Parallel World Ticking

Ticks each world on its own thread, keeping Paper's and Folia's tick
thread checks: only the thread bound to a world may change it.

Ported from SparklyPaper (https://github.com/SparklyPower/SparklyPaper) by
MrPowerGamerBR. SparklyPaper publishes no license file; as a modification of
GPL-3.0 Paper code that SparklyPaper distributes, it is used under GPL-3.0
(see CREDITS.md).

Shulker changes: off unless shulker.yml parallel-world-ticking.enabled.
While off the server behaves like Paper: the extra thread checks
SparklyPaper adds (block reads, chunk access, waypoints, ...), the
portal ban for non-player entities, the cross-world container refusal,
the wait-one-tick-before-opening-menus rule and the moved mid-tick
tasks are all conditional; the vanilla random-tick position generator
is kept; SaplingBlock.treeType, CraftEventFactory.sourceBlockOverride
and EntityTickList's no-argument constructor stay for NMS users. A
world's crash report is rethrown as is instead of wrapped.

